
Quant2: A program for DNA sequence analysis
        based on discriminant analysis

What is Quant2
------------------------------

Quant2 is a program for DNA sequence analysis based 
on discriminant analysis (class II quantification 
theory). Features of Quant2 are described as follows:

  - Extracting signal patterns in DNA sequences
    consisting of 2 categories (positive and negative
    samples).

  - Calculating category weights which indicate
    contribution to discrimination of 2 categories.
    (The weights are assigned to bases A, T, C, and G 
    at each position in a DNA sequence.)

  - Selecting minimum set of category weights, which 
    is significant to the discrimination, based on 
    statistical test.

  - Predicting functional sites and discriminating 
    DNA sequences using obtained category weights.


Requirements:
-------------

1) Hardware:
   - UNIX system
   - 400KB disk space

2) Software:
   - C compiler

We know that the program run on workstations from 
Sun, HP and Silicon Graphics. 


Installation:
-------------

Please unpack the distribution of the program 
inside the directory where the program should 
be located. 

  zcat Quant2.tgz | tar xvf -

When the distribution is unpacked, you have to 
configure the Makefile. The Makefile contains 
some variables that must correspond to your 
system. Now you can type:

  make 

from command line.


Files:
------

1) Document files

   COPYRIGHT, COPYRIGHT.j, Quant2.doc, README

2) Source files

   Makefile, quant2.h, eqn-sys.c, lda.c,
   main.c, xutils.c
					
3) Sample sequence data files

   positive.seq, negative.seq, test.seq


